        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11234104?u=d4f2a6778143f1e08e81b02cf2b9dd1f0b7eda07&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description and Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This pull request makes a minor wording update to the description of several legacy constants in the <code class=\"notranslate\">files/en-us/web/api/treewalker/index.md</code> documentation.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The descriptions for <code class=\"notranslate\">NodeFilter.SHOW_ENTITY</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">NodeFilter.SHOW_ENTITY_REFERENCE</code>, and <code class=\"notranslate\">NodeFilter.SHOW_NOTATION</code> have been changed from \"Legacy, no more usable.\" to \"Legacy, no longer used.\", clarifying their grammar and intent.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">N/A</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41122",
            "title": "Update deprecation messages for NodeFilter constants",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-15T23:16:09.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-14T17:33:39.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "nberlette",
                "url": "https://github.com/nberlette"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/432915?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Here's a new article on phishing attacks.</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>I went back and forth a bit on how much to talk about the details of WebAuth. Minimally we could just say \"a passkey is associated with an origin, and the browser will never allow the user to choose the passkey for the real site when the user is on the fake site\". But it felt worth talking a bit more than this.</li>\n<li>I'm not sure how much to talk about \"downsides\" of passkeys. I do feel like the tooling isn't so mature at the moment and things like passkey export are a bit unclear. But I don't know much about this (yet).</li>\n<li>I was also on the fence about including the bit on security indicators. In the end I have included it but not recommended it.</li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41115",
            "title": "New attacks article: phishing",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-17T15:39:02.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-12T21:19:33.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "wbamberg",
                "url": "https://github.com/wbamberg"
            }
        },
        {
